    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d703">

                <pb facs="0993" n="983" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg983"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/5–746: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-05-07T16:00:00+08:00">May 7, 1946—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 8—6:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>763. Representative of Embassy transmitted your message to T. V. Soong on May 6.
                    (Reurtel 58 of May 1.) Soong said he believed value inventory would be small and
                    that he would ask Dr. Wong Wen-hao to furnish required data earliest
                    possible.</p>
                <p>2. In same interview, Dr. Soong said he had instructed T. M. Hsi<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d703-f1"/> and T. L. Soong<anchor n="25" xml:id="d703-f2"/> to
                    represent China in negotiations in Washington for determination of US dollar
                    equivalent of our yuan debt to China. It was thereupon pointed out to Soong that
                    what we desire is negotiations for an overall settlement of war account between
                    US and China, of which yuan debt is only one item. General Marshall had made our
                    desire for speedy initiation of negotiations for overall settlement clear in a
                    letter to Soong dated February 20.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d703-f1" n="24" xml:id="d703-f1-content">
                <p>Hsi Te-mou, representative in the United States of the Chinese Ministry of
                    Finance and the Central Bank of China.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d703-f2" n="25" xml:id="d703-f2-content">
                <p>Brother of T. V. Soong.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
